A second card in the carousel, as a patch (Phase 5).

The Registry ships one game, so `browsingGameIndex` has nothing to move
between and the Card Transition — the 250ms ease-out §6 asks for — has nothing
to animate on a shipped build. This installs a second entry (trivia's own
module and logic under another id, title and key art) so the transition can be
driven and watched.

Both lists have to grow, and the server's is the one that is easy to forget:
`browseGame` clamps the index against `GAME_LOGIC_REGISTRY` in the Convex
deployment, so a patched client alone leaves the index pinned at 0 and the
television perfectly still.

    git apply tools/carousel-transition-repro.patch
    (cd convex && npx convex dev --once)      # the clamp lives on the server
    # drive it: convex run games:browseGame '{"sessionToken":"…","index":1}'
    git apply -R tools/carousel-transition-repro.patch
    (cd convex && npx convex dev --once)      # put the deployment back

It is a patch and not a fixture because a second game is a Registry decision
(docs/CONTEXT.md), and a hub that ships a fake one to make its animations
visible is a hub lying about what it installs.

